Fixes every leg applies (build_turnip.sh, build_turnip_perf.sh, build_turnip_wayland.sh,
build_turnip_linux.sh) through apply_common.sh, before the variant's own EXTRA_PATCH/EXTRA_SCRIPT.
They are KGSL-backend bugs, so Android builds carry them too.

mesa-44838/0001-0013 (Danylo Piliaiev, Mesa MR !44838 "tu/kgsl: A bunch of fixes for KGSL sync",
  branch Danil/mesa turnip/fix/kgsl-bunch-of-fixes at d7b5feb1, opened 2026-10-01; still open)
  Taken as-is with git format-patch, kept under his names and numbers so they can be diffed
  against the MR. Every patch touches only tu_knl_kgsl.cc and none checks the chip, so every
  driver gets them. They replace our two patches (taken out 2026-10-01):
  - 0002 "Prevent indefinite wait times for 0 timeout waits" = our kgsl-zero-timeout-poll.patch
    (The412Banner, 2026-09-29; the commit credits us). WAITTIMESTAMP_CTXTID with timeout 0 is
    KGSL's "wait forever"; vkd3d-proton's timeline polls ran CPU and GPU in lock-step. A poll
    now reads READTIMESTAMP_CTXTID (retired). Report: docs/KGSL_ZERO_TIMEOUT_POLL.md.
  - 0010 "Correctly merge timestamps and sync files" = our kgsl-syncobj-merge-ts-fd.patch
    (DroidDeck, 2026-09-26): kgsl_syncobj_merge converted the wrong syncobj when a timestamp met
    a sync file (Cemu crashed on its first frame) and mis-merged timestamps from two queues.
    Ours was device-proven with Cemu, RPCS3 and Dolphin on the Linux leg.
  - The other eleven are his: wait-any picks the earliest timestamp (0006), reads poll()
    correctly (0007) and handles FD-only waits without a NULL queue (0011); no OOB read in
    kgsl_syncobj_foreach_state (0005); no overflow in kgsl_queue_wait_fence (0004); timeouts
    always round up (0003); profiling obj leak (0012/0013); errors returned (or device lost)
    instead of asserts (0001, 0008, 0009).
  0001 also removes the assert(errno == ETIMEDOUT) in wait_timestamp_safe, so the Wayland and
  Linux legs no longer apply their own edit of it (Termux 0014): it ran first and made 0001 reject.
  Verified 2026-10-01 on Mesa main ab10c108 for every leg's recipe (Android, Wayland pre-steps,
  Linux pre-patches x Standard, A8xx + Max's series + gen8 stack, 710-720, 8G2 One UI): zero
  rejects, zero fuzz (offsets only). Drop the whole directory once !44838 is in Mesa main.

A8XX DRIVER ONLY (since 2026-09-30, after r7): ../a8xx-winnative/0001-0006 are applied by
apply_common.sh only when EXTRA_PATCH is the gen8 stack. 0001 (mesh) and 0002 (wave32) also switch
on for A7xx (0002 for A6xx gen4 too: has_getfiberid), where they can steer DX12 games onto
emulated paths (compute mesh + forced sysmem, half-wave subgroups); a user felt A7xx slower on
r6/r7. The A6xx/A7xx drivers therefore carry only mesa-44838/,
and apply_common.sh fails if tu_mesh.cc reaches a non-A8xx driver.

a8xx-winnative/0001-0006 (Max / MaxsTechReview, WinNative-Emu/Drivers linux/patches, GPL-3.0;
  0001-0005 2026-09-27/28, 0006 c71f600a 2026-09-29). Kept under Max's own names and numbers so
  they can be diffed against his repo; they build on each other and apply in that order, after
  mesa-44838/ (0005/0006 apply on top of it with offsets only). Replaces our earlier renamed copies of
  0003-0005 (a8xx-*.patch, 2026-09-28), which had 0004 adapted because 0001 was missing.
  - 0001 mesh shaders: VK_EXT_mesh_shader emulated with compute. Task/mesh shaders write into a
    device ring that a generated vertex shader draws; render passes with mesh draws use sysmem.
    Exposed on chip >= A7XX with >= 32 KiB compute shared memory.
    REBASED onto Mesa 4da08cb (2026-09-30): upstream folded tu_shader_serialize/deserialize into
    tu_shader_cache_process_blob(), so Max's two MESA_SHADER_COMPUTE blob hunks are one
    io.bytes(&shader->mesh) case there. At fuzz 3 the old hunks landed outside any function.
    Everything else is Max's diff unchanged.
  - 0002 wave32: a required subgroup size of 32 on A8XX's 64-wide waves (each half-wave is a
    subgroup), so vkd3d-proton accepts WaveSize(32) shaders.
  - 0003 cube-coord sanitize: a NaN/zero cube-map direction hangs A8XX; clamp NaN to 0 and turn the
    zero vector into +Z (quirk on a8xx_base only).
  - 0004 bindless invalidate: A8XX's SP_UPDATE_CNTL has no bindless bits; invalidate through
    SP_GFX/CS_BINDLESS_INVALIDATE. Older chips unchanged.
  - 0005 IB VBO alias: freeing command-stream memory with GPUMEM_FREE_ID hangs A8XX; IBs are fetched
    through a KGSL VBO alias that is unbound before the free (A8XX only).
  - 0006 IB cache: reuse retired A8XX IB BOs + aliases instead of unbind/free churn during play
    (per-device, 256 MiB idle cap, freed at device destroy). TU_KGSL_IB_CACHE=false disables it.
    Max: RedMagic A840v2 passed movement/menus/exit in FF7 Rebirth; long play + warm relaunch
    still unverified on his side.
  All six verified 2026-09-30 on Mesa 4da08cb for every leg's recipe (Standard, A8xx + gen8 stack,
  710-720, 8G2 One UI; Android, Wayland pre-steps, Linux pre-patches): zero rejects, zero fuzz.
  When Mesa moves and one stops applying, rebase it here (or pull Max's rebase) - never drop it
  silently.
